# SUMMARY
Addresses bugs with moving submodules when they're renamed.

# DETAILS
 ### Fixes

  - Detect submodule moves more reliably by parsing .gitmodules path changes, including cases where the .gitmodules section name changes
    along with the path.
  - Handle moved submodules during grape md even when there are no ordinary modified submodule gitlinks in the pre-merge diff.
  - Remap recursive merge targets from old submodule paths to new ones after the outer merge updates .gitmodules.
  - Include moved active submodules in the recursive submodule merge set so public-branch changes in those submodules are still merged.
  - Fix moveSubmodule() so it correctly handles a destination path that already exists as an empty placeholder after checkout/merge.
  - Move the submodule backend repo under .git/modules/<new-path> and rewrite the submodule .git file and core.worktree to the new
    location.
  - Handle retry/recovery cases where a stale destination backend already exists under .git/modules/<new-path> from a previous failed
    attempt.

  ### Result

  - GRAPE now moves submodules to their new paths during merge instead of leaving the real contents in the old location.
  - Recursive submodule merges continue on the new paths after the move.
  - Git commands like git status no longer fail because the moved submodule metadata still points at the old worktree.

  ### Tests

  - Added regression tests for:
      - move detection when the submodule name changes
      - moving into an empty destination placeholder
      - moving when a stale destination backend already exists
      - remapping moved submodule paths during merge
      - keeping moved active submodules in the recursive merge candidate list
